  "sampling_neutrality_verification": {
    "mechanism": "build_pilot.py sorts rows by r.id (a sha256 content digest - language- and path-independent), then applies random.Random(f'provenlattice-fidelity-v1:{repo}:{stratum}').shuffle (seeded Mersenne Twister) and takes the first N. No language, extension, or path ordering is used.",
    "conclusion": "The selection is a seeded random sample over the full stratum population; after filtering Python rows the C/C++ subsample remains interpretable as a population estimate. No deterministic path-order truncation occurred.",
    "empirical_check": "Per-stratum sample_cpp_fraction tracks population_cpp_fraction with small deviations (e.g. rocksdb CALLS_NONRESOLVED 0.900 vs 0.981; rocksdb IMPORTS_NONRESOLVED 0.800 vs 0.901; aria2 CALLS_RESOLVED 0.950 vs 0.989), with no systematic direction across the 18 strata; deviations are consistent with small-n random sampling."
  },
